Copyright (c) 2026 Sonic Field Labs and contributors.

germ is an independent open-source research tool for generative microsound,
lineage-aware audio cultivation, and Listening Stack integrations.

germ is not an official Stability AI product, is not endorsed by Stability AI,
and does not distribute Stable Audio 3 model weights. Stable Audio 3 provider
paths are optional local integrations. Users are responsible for accepting and
following the licenses, model cards, gated-weight terms, and usage restrictions
for any third-party model, checkpoint, LoRA, dataset, or generated asset they
choose to use with germ.

The optional `python-provider` extra references:

stable-audio-3 @ git+https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-3.git

That dependency is not vendored in this repository. Install it only if your use
case and environment are compatible with the upstream project and model terms.

The upstream Stable Audio 3 code repository currently identifies an MIT code
license. Stable Audio model weights use separate model terms, including the
Stability AI Community License for published Stable Audio 3 checkpoints. Those
terms are not replaced by GERM's MPL-2.0 license.

Earworm integration surfaces map germ metadata into Earworm 0.4-compatible
sessions for local provenance, consent, retention, and lineage workflows.

See docs/models-and-licensing.md for direct upstream references and the full
operator responsibility boundary.
